}}

==Enemy==
Dober P.D. is essentially a stronger [[Kory]]. He moves quite slowly with low range but sports a sizeable health pool (800,000 at 100% strength magnification) and only two knockbacks. His strong Area Attacks have a 33% chance generate a Lv.3 [[Wave Attack]] on hit. Overall, Dober P.D is a challenging enemy to defeat due to the lack of units specialized to deal with [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemies for how early he is encountered.

==Strategy==
A good way to deal with him and his wave attacks is to stack many ranged units with '''no meatshields''' so as not to trigger his waves (namely [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]], [[Gross Cat (Normal Cat)|Macho Leg Cat]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Gross Cat]], [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]], [[Crazed Lizard Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Dragon Cat]] and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]]). When supporting enemies are present, release only 1 type of meatshield, preferably one that is slow ([[Cat (Normal Cat)|Mohawk]] or [[Tank Cat (Normal Cat)|Eraser Cat]], ''maybe'' [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cats]]) so that they won't plow through your stack and that Dober P.D will occasionally miss due to other enemies destroying your meatshields.

Since Dober P.D is naturally slow, freeze and knockback effects are effective against him. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]] may help with her occasional knockbacks, and the [[Sniper the Cat]] item is recommended against him too. Later in the game, [[Glass Cat (Rare Cat)|Macho Crystal Cat]] and [[Lone Cat and Kitten (Rare Cat)|Tourist Cat]] are extremely effective, as Dober will barely even move in their presence.

[[:Category:Cats with Wave Immunity|Cats that are immune to waves]] (e.g., [[Anubis the Protector (Uber Rare Cat)|Anubis the Protector]], [[Togeluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Togelan Pasalan]]), especially those that are also [[:Category:Anti-Traitless Cats|anti-Traitless]] (such as [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]] exclusives [[Shadow Gao (Uber Rare Cat)|Shadow Gao]], [[Dark Mitama (Uber Rare Cat)|Dark Mitama]] and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]], and other "exclusive" Ubers like [[Koneko (Uber Rare Cat)|Koneko]]) are particularly useful against Dober P.D. [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] (preferably with the Immune to Waves [[Talents|Talent]]) and [[Mightycat (Rare Cat)|Supercat]] can weaken Dober to make his attacks more manageable, and [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] can survive multiple hits from Dober at weaker magnifications, allowing units like [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] and [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Dancing Flasher Cat]] to get lots of free damage on Dober. A [[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|ranged]] [[Hatsune Miku: MM2020 Tokyo (Uber Rare Cat)|Wave]] [[Yamii (Uber Rare Cat)|Shield]] is even more useful, as they can avoid Dober's attacks while still blocking waves for your melee attackers.

[[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] with a level 10 Survive Talent can prove very effective against him, especially along with her Resist Wave Talent, provided she is used in the same way you would fight against [[Kappy Jr.]] (no meatshielding combined with crowd-control units). This strategy becomes even more effective if you have "Research" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combos]], such as [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]], [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], [[Cheating Heart? (Combo)|Cheating Heart?]], and [[Kimono Champs (Combo)|Kimono Champs]]. This works because Cameraman Cat outranges Dober P.D, and her Survive ability as well as, if desired, Resist Wave Talent allows her to take a wave attack to the face. However, there are usually more effective counters for how little the expensive Resist Wave Talent does.

